Here's an accessible **skip-link pattern** using **HTML**, **CSS**, and **JavaScript**:

### ✅ Skip-Link Pattern (HTML + CSS)

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <title>Accessible Skip-Link</title>
  <style>
    body {
      font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0;
    }

    .skip-link {
      display: none;
      position: absolute;
      top: -50px;
      left: 50%;
      transform: translateX(-50%);
    }

    .skip-link.active {
      display: block;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>

<!-- Skip Link -->
<div class="skip-link" id="skipLink">Skip to Top</div>

<script>
  document.getElementById('skipLink').addEventListener('click', function() {
    window.scrollTo({ top: 0, behavior: 'smooth' });
  });
</script>

```

### 📌 How It Works:

- The skip-link is hidden by default.
- When clicked, it becomes **active** and appears at the top of the screen.
- The `window.scrollTo()` method smoothly scrolls to the top of the page.

### ✅ Example Output:

When you click on the skip-link, it will scroll to the top of your browser window.

